 "post_review": "Malicious-labelled files CLEAN in both releases: 2. After the measurement was final these two files only were looked at (by scan() and a byte search; nothing was loaded): both are scikit-learn TfidfVectorizer pickles whose vocabulary holds words such as `runpy`, `urllib3` and `pathlib` taken from chat text. Their only imports are the vectorizer, its transformer and NumPy, all allowlisted, and the emulation recorded nothing. The Hub antivirus matched those strings; the files are benign, so the label is the error, not the verdict. Nothing was changed because of them."
